  "final_message": "AlmaLinux records now add an `advisory` fix entry to every range with a `fixed` event, using the UTC date from upstream `published`. Cloned library packages receive the same entries, and the record-level advisory marker remains intact. The parser accepts an optional fix date finder, works as a context manager, and downloads fix date data once per run. I also wrote [answer.json](/tmp/bsvc-919ubkus/vunnel/answer.json).\n\nAlmaLinux and Rocky tests pass (9 total), as does AlmaLinux type checking. The full suite has unrelated failures from a missing `yardstick` dependency and a sandbox permission error; full type checking reports two errors in the untouched RHEL parser.",
